1
00:00:01,030 --> 00:00:02,162
Per Weapon mode.

2
00:00:02,182 --> 00:00:03,640
Now on Xbox.

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:07,483
Most scripts give one anti-recoil per category.

4
00:00:07,503 --> 00:00:09,721
Per Weapon gives every weapon its own.

5
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:13,744
On Xbox, it reads your controller's vibration instead of a

6
00:00:13,744 --> 00:00:15,260
PS5 trigger.

7
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:19,285
You need an Xbox controller, with vibration enabled,

8
00:00:19,285 --> 00:00:22,039
on console or PC, and in the game.

9
00:00:22,289 --> 00:00:23,883
Open the Cronus menu.

10
00:00:23,903 --> 00:00:26,477
Go to Combat, Weapon Detect, and enable it.

11
00:00:26,727 --> 00:00:27,205
Press A.

12
00:00:27,205 --> 00:00:30,379
Set Device to Xbox, and Type to Per Weapon.

13
00:00:30,629 --> 00:00:32,663
Two new rows appear: Teach Weapon,

14
00:00:32,663 --> 00:00:33,824
and Tolerance.

15
00:00:34,724 --> 00:00:38,146
Unlike PS5, nothing is known out of the box.

16
00:00:38,396 --> 00:00:41,408
Until you teach a weapon, firing shows nothing.

17
00:00:41,428 --> 00:00:44,580
Your profile's manual setting is used instead.

18
00:00:45,479 --> 00:00:48,161
Open Teach Weapon, and pick an empty slot.

19
00:00:48,411 --> 00:00:50,330
Fire two or three times.

20
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:53,533
The screen shows your controller's vibration values.

21
00:00:53,783 --> 00:00:56,252
Once they're stable, confirm, pick a category,

22
00:00:56,252 --> 00:00:57,104
and save.

23
00:00:57,504 --> 00:00:59,918
Fire it again, and it claims its own slot,

24
00:00:59,938 --> 00:01:01,006
automatically.

25
00:01:01,906 --> 00:01:03,431
Too high or too low?

26
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,140
Hold LT, and press Up or Down, while firing.

27
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:08,772
It's permanent, for that exact weapon.

28
00:01:09,672 --> 00:01:11,832
Two taught weapons feel too similar?

29
00:01:11,852 --> 00:01:13,901
Hold LT, and press Left or Right,

30
00:01:13,901 --> 00:01:14,882
to switch.

31
00:01:15,782 --> 00:01:18,426
Vibration drifts more than a PS5 trigger,

32
00:01:18,446 --> 00:01:19,482
shot to shot.

33
00:01:19,732 --> 00:01:21,523
Tolerance sets the margin.

34
00:01:21,543 --> 00:01:24,413
Too tight, and a weapon just isn't recognized.

35
00:01:24,662 --> 00:01:27,534
Too loose, and it confidently applies the wrong weapon's

36
00:01:27,534 --> 00:01:28,145
setting.

37
00:01:28,395 --> 00:01:30,000
When in doubt, keep it tight.

38
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:33,698
Forty eight personal slots, kept after a power off,

39
00:01:33,698 --> 00:01:34,876
and a reflash.

40
00:01:35,276 --> 00:01:36,903
Badly tuned mid fight?

41
00:01:36,923 --> 00:01:38,635
Hold View and Y, for one second,

42
00:01:38,635 --> 00:01:40,422
to fall back to your profile.

43
00:01:41,322 --> 00:01:43,889
The full guide is on Rocket Mod dot org.

44
00:01:44,289 --> 00:01:45,094
Rocket Mod.

45
00:01:45,094 --> 00:01:45,669
Per Weapon.

46
00:01:45,669 --> 00:01:46,944
On Xbox.
